WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:10.141
- I'm not sure if you're
familiar with Andrew Yang?

00:00:10.141 --> 00:00:11.250
- [Other Speaker] Yes I am.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.030
- So there's a candidate for
President of the United States

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.079
who's platform, Andrew Yang is based

00:00:16.079 --> 00:00:19.800
in part around job loss due to automation

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.240
and also in addition the need perhaps,

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:27.360
of universal basic income
to support jobs that are,

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.270
folks who lose their
job due to automation.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:32.680
So what are your thoughts
about his concerns,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.426
him as a candidate, his ideas in general?

00:00:35.426 --> 00:00:39.373
- I think his thinking is
generally in the right direction,

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:44.410
but his approach as a
presidential candidate

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.953
may be a little bit ahead of the time.

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:51.153
I think the displacements will happen,

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.760
but will they happen soon enough

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.460
for people to agree to vote for him.

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:59.770
The unemployment numbers
are not very high yet

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:03.560
and I think he and I
have the same challenge.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:07.530
If I want to theoretically
convince people this is an issue

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.279
and he wants to become the President,

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:13.500
people have to see how
can this be the case

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.680
when unemployment numbers are low.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.330
So that is the challegne.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.310
I do agree with him on
the displacement issue.

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.010
I think the main issue is retraining.

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.220
So people need to be incented

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.180
not by just giving a monthly
$2,000 check, or $1,000 check

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.860
and do whatever they want,

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.860
because they don't have the
know how to know what to retrain

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:42.560
to go into what type of a job

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:46.160
and guidance is needed,
and retraining is needed,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.890
because historically in
technology revolutions

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:52.340
where routine jobs were displaced,
new routine jobs came up,

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.550
but with AI and automation the whole point

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.390
is replacing all routine jobs eventually

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:02.480
and AI will create jobs, but
it won't create routine jobs,

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:04.670
because if it creates routine jobs

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:06.710
why wouldn't an AI just do it.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:10.180
So therefore, the people
who are losing the jobs

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.110
are losing routine jobs.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.510
The jobs that are becoming
available are non routine jobs

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:19.130
so these the social stipend
needs to be put in place

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.870
is for the routine workers
who lost their jobs

00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:26.220
to be retrained and then take
on the job that will last

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:27.570
for that person's lifetime.

